Z||000000||crzyone||02-15-2001||05:07 AM||||Hello!  I am a "sort of" new member to the forum, but I've been reading posts for a long time.  I have 2 Fieros, one I drive daily and a restoration project.  I finally figured out how to post pictures (if all else fails, read the instructions)  This is my 85 Sport Coupe, my daily driver.  It has 144000 miles on it (230000km) and is kind of getting tired.  I bought it this last summer for $500 and it only needed a master clutch cylinder, it is a blast to drive and for $500 how can you go wrong?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2M4_Front_1.jpg"> <P>I also have an 86GT restoration project.  The owner I bought it off of had a rollover in it  (country roads in the winter while drunk).  When I first found it, it was sitting with 90% of the bodywork done, but the owner had left the passenger side door off for a year.  The interior needs some work and the body needs a paint job.  He did, however, rebuild the motor and transmission, reason being is he used to rev it to high before shifting gears so he blew the engine.  The GT has 72000 miles on it (115000km) which I think is pretty low for a 15 year old car.  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Back_86GT.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side_86GT.jpg"> <P>there it is, looks rough now, but by summer I hope to have her blasting down the highway.   This was very long, sorry, I just never properly introduced myself.<P>Thanks <BR>Levi||||reg||1
